   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Hefin,<div><br></div><div>When I remove coord_polar(), I find that there is no bin corresponding to that line. You have the two tall bars (near 30 counts), then the shorter (near 10) and that’s it. It kind of looks like an artifact of the right edge of the bar.</div><div><br></div><div>It’s been a long time since I created windrose plots, but I seem to recall having problems with geom_histogram(). I have some code for a 360º windrose that works without drawing artifacts, but it uses geom_bar() instead of geom_histogram(), and scale_x_discrete() instead of scale_x_continuous(). I have to bin the data manually.</div><div><br></div><div>Regards,</div><div><br></div><div>Tom</div><div><br><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On 201611 18, at 12:24, Hefin Rhys &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hefin....@bath.edu</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
